    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2TnNAcXGicURimMfGCkPJu2)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on `main`; no dependency on other open PRs.\n- Optional: #453 (emureader, `sp-pdf-open`). Merged before this, the PDF opens in emureader; otherwise it opens with `find-file`. Either order works.\n- Touches `sp-devonthink-browse` and `sp-litnotes-meta` (small guard, see below); may conflict textually with #452 and #451 only in tests if they edit the same files.\n\n## What it does\n\n- New module `sp-fetch-inbox` (doc: `docs/tangles/academic/sp-fetch-inbox.org`), `M-x sp-fetch-inbox` or `C-c w b a`.\n- Items: records of the `inbox` group in DEVONthink `literature`, plus PDFs in `~/Documents/literature/inbox/` (`mac-bibdesk/` skipped).\n- Asks for the `.bib` file, reads the DOI from the first two PDF pages (`pdftotext`), fetches the entry with org-ref, generates the key with the `bibtex-autokey` scheme (letter suffix if taken).\n- Shows the PDF left and an editable BibTeX buffer right. `C-c C-c` files, `C-c C-k` aborts, `C-c C-r` new key, `C-c C-d` fetch another DOI.\n- After one yes/no question: PDF moved to `~/Documents/literature/KEY.pdf`, DEVONthink record renamed `KEY.pdf` and moved to the literature group, `file` field added, entry appended to the `.bib` and saved. Nothing changes before the question.\n- Embark: `f` on a DEVONthink record files it.\n\n## Also fixed\n\n- `embark-act` on a record that is not a citekey yet (e.g. `Marx_after_Hegel_...`) with the note action gave `sp-litnotes-meta: No BibTeX entry ... in the registered files`. `sp-devonthink-record-note` now says the record has no BibTeX entry and points to `sp-fetch-inbox`; `sp-litnotes-meta--after-create` skips keys without an entry.\n\n## Not run\n\n- The DEVONthink JXA (list inbox group, rename, move, export, trash) has not been run on the Mac. The move step reads the path back and stops before touching the `.bib` if the file is not at the destination.\n- `pdftotext` (poppler) is needed for DOI detection; without it the entry starts empty.\n- ERT: 14 new tests plus one for the note guard, all passing in Emacs 29.3 (DEVONthink faked).\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] `M-x sp-fetch-inbox` with one PDF in `~/Documents/literature/inbox/` and DEVONthink closed: layout is PDF | BibTeX, entry filled from the DOI\n- [ ] Same with a PDF without a DOI: empty `@article`, header says no DOI; fill it, `C-c C-r` makes a key\n- [ ] `C-c C-d` with a DOI replaces the entry\n- [ ] `C-c C-k` leaves the file and DEVONthink untouched\n- [ ] `C-c C-c`, answer `n`: nothing changes\n- [ ] `C-c C-c`, answer `y`: PDF at `~/Documents/literature/KEY.pdf`, entry at the end of the chosen `.bib` with a relative `file` field\n- [ ] With an indexed record in the DEVONthink `inbox` group: record is named `KEY.pdf`, sits in `literature`, keeps its UUID and tags, file moved\n- [ ] With an imported record: new indexed record `KEY.pdf`, offered to trash the old one\n- [ ] Two articles in the inbox: \"Next article?\" continues\n- [ ] `embark-act` on an inbox record, `n`: clear message instead of the BibTeX error; `f` starts filing\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi8mSFguF5ghQjmfQgM)_",
